Package: gmrfs
Type: Package
Title: Adaptive Gaussian Markov Random Field Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Esmail", "Abdul Fattah",
           email = "esmail.abdulfattah@kaust.edu.sa",
           role  = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Havard", "Rue", role = "ctb",
           comment = "R-INLA code in src/cgeneric.h, R/pc-bym.R and R/graph.R"),
    person("The R-INLA project", role = "cph",
           comment = "src/cgeneric.h, R/pc-bym.R and R/graph.R, see inst/COPYRIGHTS")
  )
Description: Latent Gaussian Markov random field models with adaptive
    precision structure: a Besag model and a BYM2 model with partitioned
    precisions, and collapsed, partial and stacked block models with
    shrinkage priors on the block scales. The precision matrix, mean,
    hyperparameter prior and normalising constant of each model can be
    evaluated directly from R, for use in custom samplers or optimisers.
    The same models can be used as latent components in 'INLA' through its
    'cgeneric' interface. Also provides an orthogonal matching pursuit
    screen for selecting active blocks.
